{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"test dataset test dataset","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","fileName":"Test Dataset.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Test Dataset","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Neural Network Training]] · [[Statistical Learning and Validation]] · [[Predictive Data Partitioning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Predictive Data Partitioning","Training Dataset","Overfitting","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"test dataset test dataset","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","fileName":"Test Dataset.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Test Dataset","heading":"Test Dataset","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A test dataset is a collection of examples withheld from machine-learning training and used afterward to evaluate performance on unseen data. It checks whether behavior learned from the [[Training Dataset]] transfers beyond the examples used to adjust parameters.\n\nStrong training performance paired with weak test performance is evidence of [[Overfitting]]. Because the model must not learn from the test answers during fitting, the test collection functions as an independent check rather than another training epoch.\n\nThe source uses held-out tissue samples to estimate misclassification error after a prediction rule has been trained. A sample cannot provide an honest test if its label or feature pattern was used to choose the fitted parameters being evaluated.\n\nThe book reserves the test partition for evaluation after model structure, tuning choices, and thresholds have been settled with training and validation data. This sequencing protects the final estimate from development feedback.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Predictive Data Partitioning","Training Dataset","Overfitting","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"test dataset test dataset","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Test Dataset.md","fileName":"Test Dataset.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Test Dataset","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Predictive Data Partitioning","Training Dataset","Overfitting","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}